text:
Maria Gomez: customer escalation from AcmePayments — they see the streaming /v1/streams response cut off after ~1200 tokens. client receives a partial JSON object and then an 'event: close' or the connection just drops. when the client reconnects it sometimes gets the remainder appended, sometimes gets a duplicate prefix. happened after they upgraded to our JS SDK v1.4.2. Correlation-ID: acme-req-9f3b. ticket: #12487.

Dave Liu: thanks Maria. any quick repro steps from the customer? node or browser?

Maria Gomez: Node 14 (heroku), using eventsource polyfill (eventsource package). minimal repro they provided: uses our SDK's streaming helper that wraps EventSource. they call `client.streamChat()` and then iterate events with `onmessage`. here's their snippet:

```
const es = new EventSource(url, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${TOKEN}` } });
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(e.data);
  // handle partial tokens
};
es.onerror = (err) => console.error('es err', err);
```

They said sometimes `e.data` is truncated (partial JSON) and the next event is either the remainder or a repeated prefix.

Samir Patel: I saw a similar report last week but it was in Python iterator where the async generator yielded duplicates after a reconnect. could be a server-side chunking/regenerator bug or SDK buffering regression in v1.4.2. do we have runtime logs correlated to acme-req-9f3b?

Jen SRE: digging. I pulled logs from runtime for acme-req-9f3b across hosts. I see a 502 from proxy at 2026-03-12T14:22:13Z for that connection, then a 200 when the reconnect happened. proxy logs show `upstream prematurely closed connection` and then a retry. payloads around that time show chunked transfer-encoding with chunks ending mid-utf8 sequence. possible bug: our flush boundary cuts in-flight multi-byte token sequences.

Support Bot: <log-attachment:acme-req-9f3b-raw.txt> (uploaded)

Maria Gomez: customer also reported that they see the behavior only with EventSource polyfills on Node; browser clients are fine. they said downgrading SDK to v1.4.0 removed the issue.

Dave Liu: important: v1.4.2 included the streaming buffer change to 'emit-on-newline' for efficiency. that could explain partial JSON if chunk boundaries no longer align with event separators. check PR #4207.

Samir Patel: reproducer plan: run a local Node14 app using eventsource package + SDK v1.4.2 against staging runtime with proxy settings to simulate premature close. add a small shim that concatenates events and attempts JSON.parse on each e.data to trigger truncation errors. I'll try to reproduce with `ab` or `wrk` to cause abrupt upstream closes.

Jen SRE: additional info — proxy uses 10s keepalive; if backend stalls, it issues a RST. my logs show backend returned `data: {"delta":"hello` then connection closed, client gets `data: {"delta":"hello` (no closing brace). reconnect uses Last-Event-ID? our streaming implementation does not currently persist event ids for resume, and SDK doesn't set Last-Event-ID on reconnect. that could explain duplication vs continuation behavior.

Maria Gomez: customer asked for mitigation: can we advise them to set a shorter keepalive or switch to long-polling? they prefer streaming; they asked if there's a recommended client-side workaround.

Dave Liu: immediate mitigation suggestions: 1) on client, buffer partial `e.data` fragments and attempt to merge with next event if JSON.parse fails — add a small retry/concat loop. 2) use exponential backoff and dedupe by server-provided token if present. 3) pin SDK to 1.4.0 for now.

Samir Patel: long-term fix options: A) server: send event ids and include resumable offset so clients can send Last-Event-ID to resume mid-stream without duplicates. B) server: ensure chunk boundaries never split UTF-8 sequences (use flush alignment) and avoid splitting JSON objects across chunk flushes for SSE events. C) SDK: change v1.4.2 behavior to keep existing buffering semantics and emit full event lines only after newline + complete JSON parse.

Eng Runtime Bot: ping @eng-runtime-team — possible regression in streaming flush/encoder since the new kernel selector landed.

Jen SRE: I will run a targeted repro: patch the proxy to drop after X bytes to mimic premature close, capture raw TCP and HTTP chunks, and produce a failing test script.

Dave Liu: I'll open an urgent bug in our repo referencing customer ticket #12487 and link to the logs and repro. label: P0-streaming-regression. assign to eng-runtime. include note about Node polyfill interaction.

Maria Gomez: customer is sensitive to any data duplication (financial notices). they want an ETA. can we get a hotfix timeline?

Samir Patel: if it's a small SDK revert we can ship a patch release (1.4.3) within 24 hours. if server-side kernel/flush change needed, that may be 3–5 days including canary. proposing: release SDK 1.4.3 that restores previous buffering behavior and adds a configurable `streaming.fragmentBufferMs` flag for Node polyfills. in parallel, eng-runtime investigates chunk flush alignment.

Jen SRE: agree. I'll prioritize the runtime investigation and prepare a canary with stricter flush boundaries.

Dave Liu: temporary handoff to eng-runtime. Maria, please tell the customer: 1) we're shipping an SDK patch (1.4.3) within 24h as a workaround; 2) ask them to pin to 1.4.0 or wait for 1.4.3; 3) recommend client-side concat-on-fail as a stopgap and share minimal snippet.

Maria Gomez: copying suggested snippet for concat:

```
let pending = '';
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  try {
    const payload = JSON.parse(pending + e.data);
    pending = '';
    handle(payload);
  } catch (err) {
    pending += e.data; // accumulate until valid JSON
  }
};
```

Maria Gomez: customer accepted that and asked for patched SDK so they can upgrade safely. I'll mark the ticket as escalating to eng-runtime and include the logs.

Eng Runtime Bot: created issue runtime#6789 (P0) with logs and repro; assigned to @samir.

Samir Patel: taking. first action: reproduce locally; second: write a unit test in the runtime that asserts chunk boundaries do not break UTF-8 codepoints; third: coordinate SDK revert/patch.

Jen SRE: note for postmortem: consider adding i/o-level integration tests that simulate abrupt upstream close and validate SSE semantics end-to-end. also consider adding Last-Event-ID support and guidance for SDKs.

Dave Liu: will draft customer-facing timeline and coordinate with Maria.

Maria Gomez: thanks everyone. I'll update the customer thread with the SDK pin and workaround. please post status updates here. :thumbsup:
